  {
   "path": "SCENE.md",
   "role": "instructions",
   "content": "# Duotone Beat\n\nA two-ink halftone portrait that swaps its ink pair on every beat, punches in on the downbeat and shows a bar indicator. A built-in silhouette stands in for the photo; a host replaces the contents of the .db-picture layer with its own image.\n\nCategory: graphic-looks. Length: 4 s. WebGL: no.\n\nUse when:\n- A speaker, artist or team portrait should hit on the beat of a track, poster-style, for a promo or social cut.\n- The edit is cut to music at a known BPM and the visual should flash through brand color pairs in time.\n- A photo needs a bold two-color print treatment that keeps moving instead of sitting as a still.\n\nAvoid when:\n- The print look should hold steady on a live scene with full color separation: use halftone-print.\n- The image should print once and settle, without a beat: use two-ink-print.\n- The beat should drive a camera jolt on heavy content rather than a color swap: use impact-shake.\n\nVariables:\n- beat_frames (number, 4-30): Frames per beat, default 15\n- beats_per_bar (number, 1-8): Beats per bar, default 4\n- punch (number, 0-0.2): Punch, default 0.07\n- halftone (number, 0-20): Halftone pitch, default 8\n- show_indicator (boolean): Bar indicator, default true\n- palettes (string): Ink pairs, default \"[[\\\"#111111\\\",\\\"#FFFFFF\\\"],[\\\"#111111\\\",\\\"#E5322D\\\"],[\\\"#E5322D\\\",\\\"#FFFFFF\\\"],[\\\"#E5322D\\\",\\\"#111111\\\"]]\"\n- speed (number, 0.1-4): Speed, default 1\n\nSource: https://github.com/Remocn/remocn. Licence: MIT. The scene file keeps the upstream notice.\n"
  },
